  nonce: '32e1'  # 32e1
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-28 at dev 5f80a79081. PREMISE HOLDS, THE SCOPE IS WIDER, AND THE FREQUENCY IS NOW MEASURED. Record: scratchpad johib/.\n\n1. REPRO, shipped survey, one file (class HealthServer defines root and read; module Postal, class Config defines only self.other):\n     Rails.root.join(\"lib\")   -> HealthServer#root   (undeclared constant, as filed)\n     Postal::Config.root      -> HealthServer#root   (a DECLARED constant that does not define the method: the row's parenthetical, confirmed)\n     File.read(p)             -> HealthServer#read   (a STDLIB I/O call captured by a same-named project method)\n   All carry receiver=generic.\n\n2. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE RUBY OVERLAY (WI-guhuv), measured. Ruby ships 0 catalogue rows, so this bites once a user supplies one. With --io-primitives rowing File.read as fs_read, a must_not_exist fs_read claim:\n     file with only File.read(p)                            VIOLATED (control)\n     same call in a repo that defines some other #read      INCONCLUSIVE ('calls into 1 module(s) ... could not classify (HealthServer)')\n   The finding is lost and the gate blames a project class. Withholding, not a false clean, but a user's own overlay row is defeated by an unrelated method name.\n\n3. FREQUENCY on postal. Instrument: the shipped survey's calls edges into in-repo METHOD nodes, joined to the source line with a regex for Const(::Const)*.method. The regex and the join are hand-built, not a shipped scan.\n     160 constant-receiver calls land on an in-repo method\n      54 land on a DIFFERENT class than the constant names (34%): 43 through a constant the repo does not declare, 11 through one it declares\n      23 more are chained (Const.x.m), not classified\n   Random sample: Postal::Config.dns -> DNSResolver#dns (x5), ActiveRecord::Base.connection_pool -> Database#connection_pool, Rails.root -> HealthServer#root, User.find -> Message.find, Server.find -> Message.find, Regexp.escape -> Database#escape, SecureRandom.uuid -> Request#uuid, Postal::Config.message_db -> Server#message_db.\n   NOT checked: inheritance. The owner comparison is by last constant segment only, so a method genuinely inherited from a declared base class could be counted wrong; none in the sample is."  # 32e1
